# MEASUREMENT PROBE — the spine study, worktree-only, never to be landed.
#
# `git apply scripts/spine-probe.diff` onto a scratch worktree, then
#
#   cargo build --release --features nanoda_lib/stepcount,nanoda_lib/tg --bin nanoda_bin
#   ./target/release/nanoda_bin cfg.json 2>&1 | grep PROBE      # census, side-effect free
#   NANODA_SPINE_EXPERIMENT=1 …                                 # rebuild + ask, result discarded
#   NANODA_SPINE_EXPERIMENT=1 NANODA_SPINE_FIX=1 …              # …and returned, so the ledger speaks
#
# What it adds, all under `#[cfg(feature = "stepcount")]`:
#
#   * `Shared::typed_subj_ty` — one representative *target* per subject, so
#     "was this term ever typed" can be followed by "at what". `typed_subj`
#     answers the first; a function-space route needs the second.
#   * `TgBackend::spine_probe` — at every `TmStep::NoNode`, peels the subject's
#     application spine to its atom head and counts: spine length, what the
#     atom head is, whether each leaf has a Lean node, and which of the facts a
#     function-space route would need the thread actually holds.
#   * The experiment: rebuild the missing application node from the leaves with
#     `foldl_apps`, check it interprets to the subject, and ask the ordinary
#     `has_type` recursion about it. Off unless `NANODA_SPINE_EXPERIMENT` is
#     set, because it derives.
#
# The census half is side-effect free: with the experiment off, `init-prelude`'s
# whole ledger is byte-identical (15734 gaps, 2232 escapes, 159803 derived).
# See MEASUREMENTS.md, "beta's own domain premise is not a blocker", for the
# numbers and the verdict.
